WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.265 --> 00:00:01.380
MARK MIRCHANDANI:
What's up, everyone.

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:02.755
Thanks for checking
out This Week

00:00:02.755 --> 00:00:05.465
in Cloud, where we serve
you the lowest latency news.

00:00:05.465 --> 00:00:07.340
March is a special month,
because it contains

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.430
one of our favorite days--

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:09.440
Pi Day.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:10.940
In honor of the
occasion, we set out

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:13.357
to break the world record for
the highest number of digits

00:00:13.357 --> 00:00:17.210
calculated and we got there--
with 31.4 trillion digits.

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:19.430
But in all fairness, we
had one big advantage--

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:20.750
Google Compute Engine.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:22.710
With built-in features
like live migration,

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:24.890
we could continue running
the calculations non-stop

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:27.950
over the 118 days it
took without any downtime

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:29.720
for infrastructure updates.

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:32.390
Read about the history behind
algorithms that calculate pi

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:34.880
and what we had to do
differently all on the GCP

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:36.260
blog.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:38.060
Speaking of March
Madness, Google Cloud

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:39.650
has teamed up with
the NCAA again

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:41.548
to bring big data to basketball.

00:00:41.548 --> 00:00:44.090
If you've been looking for an
edge in your bracket this year,

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:47.190
try out this NCAA
BigQuery Qwiklab.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:49.920
This lab gets you hands on with
BigQuery, using a huge data

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:52.382
set of basketball
statistics and even gets

00:00:52.382 --> 00:00:54.590
you started building a
machine learning model capable

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:57.182
of making smart predictions
like your friends never could.

00:00:57.182 --> 00:00:58.640
Try it out for
yourself and improve

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:00.433
your bracketology skills.

00:01:00.433 --> 00:01:01.850
You may have heard
the recent news

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:03.710
about Google's
console-free game streaming

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:05.269
platform called Stadia.

00:01:05.269 --> 00:01:08.570
But, even before that, the cloud
was helping to reinvent gaming.

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:11.510
Read about how high availability
and rapidly scalable compute,

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:14.030
built into GCP, allowed
multi-player breakout

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:17.570
hit, "Apex Legends," to reach
a whopping 50 million users

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:19.087
in just under a month.

00:01:19.087 --> 00:01:21.420
Thanks to Google Cloud Platform
and open-source services

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:24.200
like Agones and Open Match, it's
never been easier to host games

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:25.410
in the cloud.

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:27.893
So, if you've got an idea
for the next great game,

00:01:27.893 --> 00:01:29.810
learn how our partners
did it and let GCP help

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:32.370
you make your game a reality.

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:34.640
Our Google Doodle on March
20th celebrated JS Bach's

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:37.220
334th birthday,
but it also marked

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:39.170
another special
occasion-- the first time

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:41.000
AI was used a Google Doodle.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.220
Coconet, the open-source
machine learning model,

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:46.070
analyzed over 300 samples
of Bach's compositions

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:48.380
to accurately
recreate full pieces

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:49.858
from only small fragments.

00:01:49.858 --> 00:01:51.650
Check the story out to
play with the doodle

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:53.407
and download the model
to make some music.

00:01:53.407 --> 00:01:55.490
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:57.440
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:57.440 --> 00:01:58.700
Have any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:00.360
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.740
We'll see you in the cloud.

